cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formal proof or its verification software, please cite this release."
type: software
title: "A Lean proof of optimal square packing for 17 unit squares"
authors:
  - family-names: "Fitzharding"
    given-names: "Oscar"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ofitzharding/sq17-lean"
url: "https://github.com/ofitzharding/sq17-lean/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
commit: "0a7167efa8dcae7fa73855890630fb7e2de550ed"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of global optimality for John Bidwell's 1998 packing of
  seventeen unit squares in a square. The theorem proves that a packing exists
  at container side L exactly when L is at least the specified exact algebraic
  endpoint, approximately 4.675530093604551. Arbitrary independent rotations
  and boundary contact are allowed. Geometric soundness is proved in Lean;
  finite certificate checks use native_decide and trust Lean's compiler and
  native evaluator and the C toolchain. The complete source release includes
  three certificate-source archives and a clean source rebuild receipt.
keywords:
  - square packing
  - discrete geometry
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - computer-assisted proof
